'''Iziz''' was the [[capital]] [[city]] of the [[Inner Rim Territories|Inner Rim]] [[planet]] [[Onderon]]. During the [[Clone Wars]], the city was host to several battles that made up the [[Onderonian Civil War]], in which the [[Onderon rebels]], backed by the [[Galactic Republic]], overthrew the forcibly-installed [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] administration.

==Description==
Iziz served as the [[capital]] [[city]]<ref name="War Two Fronts" /> of the [[Inner Rim Territories|Inner Rim]]<ref name="Tipping Points" /> [[planet]] [[Onderon]]. It was surrounded by large walls, which protected its population from Onderon's dangerous [[jungle]]s. The primary entrance to the city was across a bridge that was defended by turrets and a [[ray shield]].<ref name="Front Runners" /> Following the [[invasion of Onderon]] during the [[Clone Wars]]<ref name="BTCTG">''[[Star Wars: Battles that Changed the Galaxy]]''</ref> and ensuing [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] rule of the city, [[B1-series battle droid|battle droids]] would search any persons who wished to enter the city.<ref name="Front Runners" />

[[File:MalganMarketTCW.png|thumb|left|240px|Iziz's Malgan Market]]
Those who entered the city were immediately thrust into the crowded courtyards of [[Malgan Market]]. Primarily [[human]]s made up the traffic in addition to [[speeder]]s and riding beasts such as the [[tee-muss]] or the [[fambaa]].<ref name="Front Runners" /> At the center of the city was the [[Unifar Temple]],<ref name="Soft War EG">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/the-soft-war-episode-guide|text="The Soft War" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref> the palace of the [[Onderonian]] [[Monarchy|monarchs]].<ref name="War Two Fronts" /> In addition to being the tallest building in the city, the temple sat slightly above the main group of buildings. A gradual slope naturally led occupants from the main marketplaces near Iziz's entrance towards [[Yolahn Square]], which was right at the foot of the temple. At the edge of the city, the [[Onderon power generator|main power generator]] was guarded by another wall. Iziz had little vegetation, but some ferns did decorate the outsides of various buildings.<ref name="Front Runners" />

Architecturally, Iziz made use of rigid lines, prominent in the rectangular nature of most of the buildings in addition to pyramidal structures like the Unifar Temple, as well as arches, which were a common style for doorways or other entrances. Furthermore, some buildings included pillars. Many of the buildings were light or dark [[Color|brown]] and had blue roofs. The Unifar Temple had a blue and yellow color scheme.<ref name="Front Runners" />

==History==
[[File:Separatists_on_Onderon.png|thumb|right|280px|The Separatist Droid Army at Iziz's main gates]]
During the Clone Wars, Iziz was occupied by the Confederacy of Independent Systems after [[King]] [[Sanjay Rash]] allied with them. A large number of B1-battle droids, [[B2-series super battle droid]]s, [[DSD1 dwarf spider droid]]s, [[droideka]]s,<ref name="Front Runners" /> and later, [[BX-series droid commando|commando droids]] and [[HMP droid gunship]]s<ref name="Tipping Points" /> were stationed in Iziz in addition to vehicles such as the [[Multi-Troop Transport]] and the [[Armored Assault Tank Mk I|Armored Assault Tank]].<ref name="Front Runners" /> Rash's actions led the [[Onderon rebels]] to oppose him,<ref name="War Two Fronts" /> eventually becoming active in Iziz to [[Onderonian Civil War|overthrow]] Rash and restore the former king, [[Ramsis Dendup]], to the throne.<ref name="Front Runners" />

==Behind the scenes==
The city of Iziz first appeared in the [[1993]] [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] comic [[Star Wars: Tales of the Jedi – Ulic Qel-Droma and the Beast Wars of Onderon|''Tales of the Jedi: Ulic Qel-Droma and the Beast Wars of Onderon'']].<ref name="Two Fronts Trivia">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/a-war-on-two-fronts-trivia-gallery|text="A War on Two Fronts" Trivia Gallery}}</ref> It went onto appear prominently in the [[2004]] video game ''[[Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic II: The Sith Lords]]''.<ref name="KOTOR2">''[[Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic II: The Sith Lords]]''</ref> The city was brought into [[canon]] in "[[A War on Two Fronts]]," the second episode of the [[The Clone Wars: Season Five|fifth season]] of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''.<ref name="Two Fronts Trivia" />

